{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792871653,"nonce":"8UMGyMkDOYEN4NeWZdDzzXbZxSI=","title":"TypeScript: ambient classes as types; class objects as values are gaps","message":"Ambient classes (declare class, and every class in a .d.ts file) were Unsupported. One is now declared as a type with fields, methods, accessors and statics whose bodies and values lie outside the program: instance fields can be read, and constructing it, calling its methods or accessors, reading its statics or extending it report Unsupported. A member without a body or return type is TypeScript's 7010. Separately, a class name used as a value (const k = C, x instanceof C, C.method = ...) reported a false 'cannot find name'; it is now Unsupported. Baseline corrections: classConstructorAccessibility3 and staticMemberAssignsToConstructorFunctionMembers passed by coincidence on that false error (the reference rejects them with 2322 elsewhere) and are now Unsupported; instanceofOperatorWithInvalidStaticToString, which the ambient class change would otherwise have turned into a false rejection, stays Unsupported.","files":null}]}